    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 42 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**, including the three new Cp29 postcode tests.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented an optional, region-validated `postcode` field for owners across the OfficeFloor create pipeline.\n\n**Contract (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)** \u2014 added a `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (4-digit string, no `required` entry so it stays optional). Since `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, it's automatically stored and returned. This drives the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`.\n\n**Entity (`model/Owner.java`)** \u2014 added a `postcode` field mapped to a `postcode` column plus getter/setter. MapStruct maps it by name in both directions (request\u2192entity, entity\u2192response) with no mapper changes needed.\n\n**Schema** \u2014 added a `postcode VARCHAR(4)` column to all four DB schemas (hsqldb \u2014 used by the tests \u2014 plus h2, postgres, mysql).\n\n**Validation (`rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerFields.java`)** \u2014 postcode is checked only when present (null/blank is accepted, keeping the request backward-compatible). A malformed (non-4-digit) value, or a well-formed value outside its city's region range, is added to the field errors and surfaces as a 400 via the existing `MissingFieldsException`. The range table (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) is keyed off the existing `Localities.region(city)` helper; a city with no known region (`UNKNOWN`) accepts any 4-digit postcode.\n\nI scoped this to the `POST /api/owners` create pipeline, which is where the specification and the acceptance suite (`AcceptanceBase` / `Cp29Tests`) exercise the rule; the PUT pipeline uses a separate validator and was intentionally left untouched.",
